@startuml Amdox-ERP-Activity
title Amdox ERP — Activity Diagram (Create User with RBAC)

' What this shows: the exact checks a request passes on its way in, and the
' HTTP status returned if any check fails. This same guard chain protects
' every write endpoint in the app.

start
:User sends POST /api/v1/users;

:authenticate (verify JWT);
if (Token valid?) then (no)
  :Return 401 Unauthorized;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (Has 'user:create' permission?) then (no)
  :Return 403 Forbidden;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Validate request body (Zod schema);
if (Body valid?) then (no)
  :Return 400 Bad Request;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Check email unique within tenant;
if (Email exists in tenant?) then (yes)
  :Return 409 Conflict;
  stop
else (no)
endif

partition "DB Transaction (tenant-scoped)" {
  :Hash password (bcrypt);
  :INSERT user (with tenantId);
  :Assign roles (UserRole);
}
:Return 201 Created;
stop

note right
  Order matters:
  auth -> permission -> validate -> business rules.
  Cheapest / most security-critical checks run first.
end note
@enduml
